markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Meet the Snack Model Code

Your students write very little code in this lab, and that is on purpose. They change one word and watch a model's decisions change. Before you try it, look at everything they will see.

<div style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; margin:20px 0;">
  <iframe
    src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/AIFY2/unit-2/snack-code-explorer.html"
    width="100%"
    height="660"
    frameborder="0"
    scrolling="no"
    title="Annotated tour of the student snack model code">
  </iframe>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#128161; Teacher tip:</b> the lab's single learning target is choosing a characteristic and seeing how that choice changes which snacks win. Encourage your students to try at least three different characteristics before they decide on a best model.</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #FFE3CE; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#9888;&#65039; Watch for:</b> the characteristic name has to match exactly, like "allergen_count" with the underscore. If your students see an error after changing the quoted word, check the spelling and capitalization first.</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 20px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">
    <img src="https://images.code.org/5ec7d742efa4da97d9ae60b79611ef3d-image-1790625929941.png" alt="Microsoft Foundry logo" style="width: 24px; height: 24px; vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 6px;"> <strong>AI-901 connection:</strong> The exam asks students to describe accountability and transparency considerations in an AI solution. Interpretability, being able to explain why a model decided what it did, supports both.
  </div>
</div>
MARKDOWN
